The following are not licensed under the MIT License, and no licence is
granted for them beyond the limited permission below. Victor Pflüger reserves
all other rights to them.

  - The name "Victor Pflüger" used as a mark.
  - His portrait photographs, including the files in assets/brand/. Rights
    that belong to the photographer stay with the photographer.
  - The Vertex logo with its lockups, app icon and favicon, the monogram
    options, the "Victor Pflüger" and "Vici" wordmarks, and the archived logo
    concepts, in any form: the files in assets/logo/, the outlines in
    src/brand/, and scripts/lib/logos.mjs, the file that draws them. That file
    is reserved as a whole, because its coordinates and colours are the
    designs.

Permission: you may show these items unchanged to refer to Victor Pflüger or to
this project, for example next to a link, in a citation or in a review, and you
may run this repository's build, which uses scripts/lib/logos.mjs, to produce
its own files. You may not use them as, or as part of, your own logo, product
name or brand, and you may not use them in a way that suggests that he made,
endorses or is affiliated with your work. If you build on Vici, put your own
name, photo and logo in their place, and replace scripts/lib/logos.mjs with your
own file or remove it from scripts/build.mjs.


